/// M09 CORE-020 "format: roots green before formatting".
/// Source: tests/integration/format_test.go symbol
/// TestFormatPreservesExecution (L35-150).
/// Related fixture: none (related_sources empty); the staged
/// src/main.can is written from the inline formatMessy const
/// (Go L15-31) at L63.
/// Disposition: RETAIN (migrate row; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment and
/// control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): static assert inventory of the staged format
/// project as the green baseline: canlc assert exits 0 with empty
/// diagnostics, the JSON report passes, and exactly 2 roots stand
/// (tally sample + pair).
/// Facet map (format_test.go legs plus fixture arms): assert-green pins
/// the before-format assert exit (L112-115: code 0, empty stderr);
/// report-passed pins the decoded report (L99: Passed true; L103-106:
/// every root passed); root-count pins the total (L28-29: sample and
/// pair, 1 + 1 = 2); fixture-name grounds the pins in the staged path
/// (L63: src/main.can; the const itself is inline at L15-31 with no
/// external fixture file); tally-roots pins the per-function count
/// (L28: sample 1 => ok 2; L29: pair 3 => ok 6; 2 roots).
/// The after-format root-identity comparison lives in
/// core-020-format-semantics.can (roots-retained, root-identities);
/// the production process shape lives in
/// core-020-run-shape.can.
/// Variants: none in this file (default only); the messy valid source,
/// second pass and syntactically invalid source live in the
/// format-semantics file.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE only; the Go test stages no sandbox
/// profile and pins no sandbox shape, so requires carries just
/// can-bun-archive. Logical gates SUITE/WORK/PROC/N1 and C/R/N/S/A
/// identities bind at P23; no live run now. Descriptor timeout
/// 120000ms mirrors the Go 2-minute ctx (L41).
/// Delegated oracles: none.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23 unmet).
/// Case format/format-roots checks: assert-green, report-passed,
/// root-count, fixture-name, tally-roots.
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.
